course: dictionary
lesson: 2749
title: Disappear, and what it can mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word disappear means to go out of sight, so you can no longer see something. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning fits. «Your suitcase disappears behind a rubber curtain at check-in» means it goes out of view through the curtain, not that it vanishes for ever.
explain: Disappear can also mean to stop existing. «The Maya did not disappear» means the Maya people did not die out. Millions still live in the same lands and speak Mayan languages today. The clues here are «still live» and «speak», so the meaning is about existing, not about going out of sight.
explain: Disappear can mean something has been lost or taken and cannot be found. Try your meaning in the sentence and check. «The southern corroboree frog almost disappeared» means it nearly died out, because the zoos work to save it. A dictionary can confirm the meaning if you are still unsure.
fact: Disappear is a verb, so it can change: disappears, disappeared, disappearing.
fact: The noun is disappearance: the act of disappearing or going missing.
fact: «Disappear» means to go out of sight so that you can no longer be seen.
fact: «Disappear» can also mean to stop existing or to be lost, as in «the dinosaurs disappeared long ago».
fact: Phrases: disappear from view, disappear into thin air, and vanish, which means the same as disappear.
exercise: «Your suitcase disappears behind a rubber curtain at check-in.» What does disappears mean here? | Makes a loud noise | Gets bigger and heavier | *Goes out of sight | Falls to the floor
exercise: «The southern corroboree frog almost disappeared.» What does almost disappeared mean? | *Nearly died out, so very few were left | Fell fast asleep for a long time | Changed its colour to yellow and black | Got very big and loud
exercise: In science, sugar disappears in water but is still there. What does this tell you? | It has been eaten up completely | It has turned into a rock | *It has gone out of sight but still exists | It has turned into a puddle for ever
test: «The Maya did not disappear: millions still live in the same lands today.» What does did not disappear mean? | Did not go to school | Did not leave their homes in the rain | Did not find any food | *Did not stop existing
test: The coin disappeared into thin air. What does disappeared into thin air mean? | Landed safely in a pocket | *Vanished, with no trace left | Was found under the table | Turned into a bird and flew away
exam: If a little child disappears from view, what should you do? | *Tell an adult straight away | Hide to see what happens next | Wait quietly where you are and say nothing | Walk off alone to look for them
